{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question","id":1006961,"title":"Grappling Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-22T19:15:36-08:00","id":1006961,"title":"Grappling Question","content":"If two characters are fighting, and the person with a higher initiative grapples the lower initiative character, does that character lose their action? In the instance I describe, the question came up because a character who was grappled and hadn't acted yet immediately opted to use a supernatural power to escape the grapple, but it brought up a good point on whether or not that's the case or not. Could such a character who was grappled use a power - shapeshifting, space blinking out, etc? I imagine you couldn't punch someone in the face after they grappled you, but curious as to people's thoughts and if this question is actually already answered in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:35:48-08:00","id":1006972,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning on allowing the grappling roll to be taken on the victim of the grapple's initiative, and afterward, if it's still engaged, use the higher initiative to roll it off.<br /> <br /> Regarding the power: Is it reflexive? if so, yes, they can use it at whichever point they wish, however many times they can, assuming they can pay their costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T19:42:18-08:00","id":1006978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question#post1006961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If two characters are fighting, and the person with a higher initiative grapples the lower initiative character, does that character lose their action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question#post1006961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the instance I describe, the question came up because a character who was grappled and hadn't acted yet immediately opted to use a supernatural power to escape the grapple, but it brought up a good point on whether or not that's the case or not. Could such a character who was grappled use a power - shapeshifting, space blinking out, etc? I imagine you couldn't punch someone in the face after they grappled you, but curious as to people's thoughts and if this question is actually already answered in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was the power? If it's Reflexive, yes, they can do it. If it requires an Instant action, no, they act on the other grappler's Initiative until the grapple ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:28:24-08:00","id":1006999,"title":"","content":"The power was break boundary. (Mage: Space 2) So no - it was not reflexive. At the time it was ruled in the means that Malus said - since the rules for grappling only state that the characters go at the highest initiative of the characters on subsequent turns, and there was nothing addressing whether the character lost their action on their <i>current </i>turn - at least that we could find at the time.<br /> <br /> Edit: And because spells can actually be cast while grappled, even if you lose that strength + brawl roll. Just couldn't find an appropriate reason that the grapple would stop the person from acting in that manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 11-22-2016, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T20:35:12-08:00","id":1007003,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd let a mage cast on their turn regardless of whether or not they were just grappled or not, because logically grappling in no way prevents them from doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:57:03-08:00","id":1007053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question?p=1007003#post1007003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd let a mage cast on their turn regardless of whether or not they were just grappled or not, because logically grappling in no way prevents them from doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This voids one of the primary tactical purposes of grappling - disabling the target. You can't take instant actions while grappled. <br /> <br /> I thought this was explicitly clarified somewhere, but I'm not seeing it in the CofD core.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:14:15-08:00","id":1007056,"title":"","content":"Mage does explicitly allow Mages to cast during grapples, but at a -3 penalty to the spell casting roll if they don't win the grapple roll. They can't incorporate Yantras that requires movement while grappled, but any Yantras used during previous turns still applies.<br /> Page 118 in Mage 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:28:28-08:00","id":1007059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question?p=1007056#post1007056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage does explicitly allow Mages to cast during grapples, but at a -3 penalty to the spell casting roll if they don't win the grapple roll. They can't incorporate Yantras that requires movement while grappled, but any Yantras used during previous turns still applies.<br /> Page 118 in Mage 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great find, and it begs the question of what other supernatural abilities belonging to other splats should be usable during a grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:43:43-08:00","id":1007063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question?p=1007056#post1007056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage does explicitly allow Mages to cast during grapples, but at a -3 penalty to the spell casting roll if they don't win the grapple roll. They can't incorporate Yantras that requires movement while grappled, but any Yantras used during previous turns still applies.<br /> Page 118 in Mage 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sensible rulings. I love it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question?p=1007059#post1007059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great find, and it begs the question of what other supernatural abilities belonging to other splats should be usable during a grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say pretty much anything that doesn't require you to do something that grappling would logically prevent should be usable. Maybe at a penalty or something, but usable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 11-23-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:49:55-08:00","id":1007065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006961-grappling-question?p=1006999#post1006999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power was break boundary. (Mage: Space 2) So no - it was not reflexive. At the time it was ruled in the means that Malus said - since the rules for grappling only state that the characters go at the highest initiative of the characters on subsequent turns, and there was nothing addressing whether the character lost their action on their <i>current </i>turn - at least that we could find at the time.<br /> <br /> Edit: And because spells can actually be cast while grappled, even if you lose that strength + brawl roll. Just couldn't find an appropriate reason that the grapple would stop the person from acting in that manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok, it being a Mage spell makes a big difference, since they're explicitly able to cast during a grapple, which is an exception to the normal grapple rules. Yeah, I'd allow it, with the -3 penalty and the restriction on movement-based Yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}